SETTLED DECISIONS (do not reopen):
* The reviewer's hostile-concurrent-writer escalation is REJECTED; option 1
  (trusted destination) stands. The ~250 lines of hand-written extern C FFI
  (openat/renameat/O_NOFOLLOW inode pinning) it produced broke 4 of 6 shipped npm
  targets (both darwin, both win32) and silently degraded the dry run there
  ('2 of 2 files differ' against a byte-identical fixture). Replaced by a portable
  atomic_copy (temp sibling + sync_all + rename), which keeps the guarantee that
  matters: never publishing a truncated DB that parses as valid-but-empty JSON and
  silently disables every type-aware diagnostic. Coordinator verified no
  extern C/openat/renameat/O_NOFOLLOW remains in src/.
* validate_refresh_destination is KEPT (refuses symlinked --into, symlinked or
  non-regular target file, the source dir itself, and ~/OpenplanetNext).
* The completions determinism fix carried in f52a007 is KEPT and needs its own
  CHANGELOG line - namespace-shortcut completions share one sortText, so
  construction order is directly observable LSP output and was inheriting HashMap
  order. f52a007's subject buries it entirely.

